/-!
# The blowup of a regular Noetherian surface at a closed point

Let `Y` be a regular Noetherian scheme with `topologicalKrullDim Y = 2` and let `y` be a closed
point of `Y`. Then the blowup of `Y` in the reduced point `{y}` is again regular of dimension
two.

[Stacks, Tag 0AGR] is the statement for the spectrum of a regular local ring `A` of dimension
two, blown up at its closed point, and that statement is formalized as
`AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_blowUp_maximalIdeal` (regularity) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.irreducibleSpace_blowUp_maximalIdeal` (irreducibility). Passing from there to a
closed point of a scheme is not formal, because **a closed point of a regular Noetherian scheme of
dimension two need not have a two-dimensional local ring**: on `Spec ℤ_p[x]` the maximal ideal
`(px - 1)` has height one, and a disjoint union of `Spec` of a field with a regular local surface
has a closed point whose local ring is a field. So the local statement has to be applied after a
case distinction on `ringKrullDim 𝒪_{Y,y}`, which the bound
`AlgebraicGeometry.ringKrullDim_stalk_le_topologicalKrullDim` confines to the values `0`, `1`
and `2`:

* dimension two is the source's case;
* in dimension one the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y,y}` is principal, generated by a nonzerodivisor,
  so the centre of the blowup of `Spec 𝒪_{Y,y}` is an effective Cartier divisor and the blowup
  morphism is an isomorphism ([Stacks, Tag 0807]);
* in dimension zero `𝒪_{Y,y}` is a field, the centre of that blowup is the zero ideal sheaf, and
  the blowup is empty — so no point of the blowup of `Y` lies over `y` at all.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isEmpty_blowUp_bot` — the blowup in the zero ideal sheaf is empty.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_and_topologicalKrullDim_le_two_blowUp_maximalIdeal` — for a regular
  local ring of dimension at most two the blowup at the closed point is regular of dimension at
  most two.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.two_le_topologicalKrullDim_blowUp_maximalIdeal` — for a regular local ring of
  dimension exactly two that blowup has dimension at least two.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_and_topologicalKrullDim_blowUp_vanishingIdeal_singleton` — the
  global statement.

## Implementation notes

Both halves of the global statement are read off the local rings of the blowup, through
[Stacks, Tag 04MU] in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_eq_iSup_krullDimOfRing_stalk`. Away from the centre the
blowup morphism is an isomorphism ([Stacks, Tag 02OS]), so its local rings there are local rings
of `Y`. Over the centre they are compared with the local rings of the blowup of
`Spec 𝒪_{Y,y}` by flat base change along `Spec 𝒪_{Y,y} ⟶ Y` ([Stacks, Tag 0805]), the comparison
morphism being a flat preimmersion and hence an isomorphism on local rings; regularity over the
centre in the two-dimensional case is exactly
`AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_blowUp_of_mapsTo`.

The lower bound `2 ≤ topologicalKrullDim` of the local statement comes from properness: the
blowup morphism of an integral Noetherian scheme in an ideal sheaf whose support is not
everything is surjective and closed, and a closed surjection does not lower the dimension
([Stacks, Tag 02JF]). The upper bound comes from birationality, [Stacks, Tag 02JX].

